esolves the core use case (being able to add key binds without using the mouse) without making a common scenario more difficult.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946594731/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946641324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625#issuecomment-3946641324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116625","id":3946641324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rPPes","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T18:49:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T18:49:50Z","body":"You can still bind Enter or escape by pressing the key if no other binding has been made yet. (I just meant it was uncommon to rebind something that was bound to escape to enter or enter to escape)\r\n\r\nBut ok we can make it so ctrl has to be held as well. What do you think about making an editor option where the default requires holding ctrl with enter/escape, but the editor option allows changing to the current behavior of this PR?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946641324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3978924361","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625#issuecomment-3978924361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116625","id":3978924361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tKZFJ","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T02:51:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T02:51:42Z","body":"> However, we can have Ctrl + Enter and Ctrl + Escape to immediately confirm/cancel. These are rarely ever bound in the input map editor. It resolves the core use case (being able to add key binds without using the mouse) without making a common scenario more difficult.\r\n\r\nI think adding Ctrl as a bind kind of complicates things. If the user has pressed \"g\", and then starts pressing ctrl with the intent of pressing enter with it to confirm the dialogue, should the fact that Ctrl is held just be stored, (without updating the listening box)? Or what if they did want to use Ctrl on its own or with a different key?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3978924361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4005609285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625#issuecomment-4005609285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116625","id":4005609285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uwL9F","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T14:49:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T14:49:55Z","body":"@Calinou Did you have thoughts on the above two comments?\r\n\r\nAlso is this something we should get the usability team involved in? (Using the mouse is required without this change)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4005609285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017017316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625#issuecomment-4017017316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116625","id":4017017316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vbtHk","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T17:51:18Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T17:51:54Z","body":"> You can still bind Enter or escape by pressing the key if no other binding has been made yet. (I just meant it was uncommon to rebind something that was bound to escape to enter or enter to escape)\r\n\r\nIn this case, I think we can leave this PR as-is is the flow is as follows:\r\n\r\n- Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> twice to bind <kbd>Enter</kbd> and confirm selection.\r\n- Press any key then <kbd>Enter</kbd> to bind the key in question, then confirm selection.\r\n- Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> then <kbd>Escape</kbd> to bind <kbd>Enter</kbd> then close the dialog, without confirming selection.\r\n- Press <kbd>Escape</kbd> then <kbd>Enter</kbd> to bind <kbd>Escape</kbd> then confirm selection.\r\n\r\n> What do you think about making an editor option where the default requires holding ctrl with enter/escape, but the editor option allows changing to the current behavior of this PR?\r\n\r\nThis isn't used very often, so I don't think we should add an editor setting for it. Adding an editor setting means we need to test twice as many workflows in terms of UX, and maintain more code for it.\r\n\r\n> I think adding Ctrl as a bind kind of complicates things. If the user has pressed \"g\", and then starts pressing ctrl with the intent of pressing enter with it to confirm the dialogue, should the fact that Ctrl is held just be stored, (without updating the listening box)? Or what if they did want to use Ctrl on its own or with a different key?\r\n\r\nTrue, I forgot that <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> can be used as a standalone key in the input map listener.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017017316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017028541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116625#issuecomment-4017028541","issue_url":"https://api.githu